      "description": "Watch Millwall vs Norwich City highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. The atmosphere at The Den reached a fever pitch as Millwall and Norwich City squared off in a highly anticipated Championship encounter. Both clubs entered the match looking to establish momentum in the early stages of the season, setting the stage for a tactical and physical battle. Arconte Sets the Tone On August 22, 2026, the referee’s whistle signaled the start of a contest that would quickly lean in favor of the home side. Millwall displayed clinical efficiency early on, breaking the deadlock in the 18th minute. Tairyk Arconte found himself in the right place at the right time to fire the ball home, giving his side a crucial lead and electrifying the home support. As the first half progressed, the physical nature of the game became apparent. A flurry of cautions followed, with Norwich City ’s Jose Cordoba and Harry Darling both entering the referee’s book. Millwall 's Jenson Metcalfe also received a yellow card shortly before the break, as both teams fought tooth and nail for every inch of grass in a tightly contested midfield scrap. Red Card and a Second for Arconte The second half saw the momentum shift decisively. In the 58th minute, Jake Cooper turned provider, delivering a pinpoint assist for Tairyk Arconte , who made no mistake in securing his second goal of the afternoon. The mountain became even steeper for the visitors in the 64th minute when Jose Cordoba was shown a second yellow card, resulting in a dismissal that left Norwich a man down for the remainder of the match . Faced with a numerical disadvantage, the Canaries attempted to refresh their lineup with multiple substitutions, but the Millwall pressure remained relentless. The tactical discipline of the hosts prevented any real chance of a comeback, as they exploited the gaps left by the shorthanded defense. Cundle Completes the Rout With the game entering its final stages, Millwall added a flourish to their performance. In the 85th minute, substitute Luke Cundle —who had replaced Kyrell Lisbie just moments earlier—latched onto a pass from Camiel Neghli to slot home the third. It was a perfect example of squad depth as the fresh legs from the bench combined to seal the result. The final whistle at 90+4' confirmed a comprehensive victory for the Lions. For Millwall , it was a statement of intent in their sports campaign, while Norwich City will head back to Carrow Road reflecting on a difficult afternoon where discipline and clinical finishing were the defining factors."
